- # `↯/s.129.1` — `Mathml.Error`
+ # `↯/s.129.1` — `Mathml.Error`

- Raised when MathML content cannot be read as the typed elements Archimedes models.
+ Levée lorsqu'un contenu MathML ne peut pas être lu comme les éléments typés que modélise Archimedes.

- ## Cause
+ ## Cause

- Archimedes represents MathML as typed elements, so an element or attribute outside the
- subset it models cannot be constructed or parsed.
+ Archimedes représente MathML par des éléments typés : un élément ou un attribut hors du
+ sous-ensemble qu'il modélise ne peut donc être ni construit ni analysé.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Code
+ column  Code

- column  Reason
+ column  Raison

- column  Message
+ column  Message

- row  `↯/s.129.1.1`  `NotMathml`  `[↯/s.129.1.1] the root element was <<label>> instead of <math>`
+ row  `↯/s.129.1.1`  `NotMathml`  `[↯/s.129.1.1] the root element was <<label>> instead of <math>`

- row  `↯/s.129.1.2`  `UnknownElement`  `[↯/s.129.1.2] the element <<label>> is not a known MathML element`
+ row  `↯/s.129.1.2`  `UnknownElement`  `[↯/s.129.1.2] the element <<label>> is not a known MathML element`

- ```
+ ```

- ## Resolution
+ ## Résolution

- Check the element against the MathML specification and against what Archimedes models.
- Presentation MathML is covered more fully than content MathML.
+ Comparez l'élément à la spécification MathML et à ce que modélise Archimedes. Le MathML de
+ présentation est couvert plus complètement que le MathML de contenu.

